      "description": "Watch ST Johnstone vs Kilmarnock highlights and goals from Premiership - Scotland on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 2, 2026. The Scottish Premiership clash on August 2, 2026 , between St Johnstone and Kilmarnock provided a spectacle that few fans will forget. Both sides entered the pitch with high ambitions, setting the stage for a match defined by momentum shifts and individual brilliance. First Half Fireworks The match began with frantic energy, and it did not take long for the deadlock to be broken. In the 16th minute, Josh Fowler latched onto a precise pass from Jamie Gullan to put St Johnstone ahead. The early goal gave the hosts confidence, but Kilmarnock refused to back down. The visitors' pressure eventually paid off in the 37th minute when Greg Kiltie , assisted by Tom Lowery , finished coolly to restore parity before the break. The half also saw its share of grit, with Tyreece John-Jules and Liam Smith picking up yellow cards. A Chaotic Start to the Second Half The beginning of the second period was absolutely chaotic, with goals coming in rapid succession. Just two minutes after the restart, Cheick Diabate put St Johnstone back in front following another Jamie Gullan assist. However, the celebration was short-lived as Joe Hugill equalized for Kilmarnock in the 49th minute. The drama intensified as defensive errors crept in; Jason Holt had the misfortune of sending the ball into his own net in the 53rd minute, briefly giving the visitors the lead. The Decisive Moment The game continued to be an emotional rollercoaster. In the 69th minute, it was Michael Schjoenning-Larsen 's turn to score an own goal, bringing the score level once again at 3-3. With the match on a knife-edge, the final hero emerged in the 80th minute. Kai Fotheringham , who had come on as a substitute, clinicaly finished a move orchestrated by Josh Fowler to seal the win. Despite late pressure and seven minutes of stoppage time, St Johnstone held on to secure the points in a true footballing classic."
